---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Delete Account"
  description="Request deletion of your Music Memory account and all associated data."
  canonical="/delete-account"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-24" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">Delete Account</h1>
      <p class="text-lg" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
        We&apos;re sorry to see you go. If you wish to delete your Music Memory account and all associated data, follow the instructions below.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-8 glass p-8 rounded-3xl border border-red-500/20 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-red-600 to-red-900" />

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">How to delete your account</h2>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-3 leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
          <li>Open Music Memory and choose <strong style="color: var(--ink)">Access &amp; Support</strong>. This option is available from the sign-in or limited-access screen and from Settings when Settings is available.</li>
          <li>Choose <strong style="color: var(--ink)">Delete Account</strong>. If needed, sign in or complete the authentication check shown by the app.</li>
          <li>Review the deletion notice and explicitly confirm the request. Your account will be scheduled for permanent deletion in <strong style="color: var(--ink)">14 days</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">What happens after you request deletion?</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Deletion remains pending during the 14-day grace period. While it is pending:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
          <li>Your profile and shared memories are hidden from other users.</li>
          <li>Signing in does not cancel deletion; your account remains in the restricted pending state.</li>
          <li>To keep your account, explicitly choose <strong style="color: var(--ink)">Cancel deletion and restore account</strong> on the pending-deletion screen before permanent deletion begins.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="leading-relaxed mt-4">
          Subscription cancellation or lapse does not delete your memories or change their selected visibility. Account deletion is a separate request that requires the confirmation above.
        </p>
        <p class="leading-relaxed mt-4">
          After the grace period, permanent deletion begins across our configured data processors. Temporary provider failures are retried. Once deletion is complete, your account and associated data — including journal entries, media files, and profile information — are permanently and irreversibly deleted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">Need help?</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          Contact <a href="mailto:support@musicmemory.app" class="hover:underline" style="color: var(--accent)">support@musicmemory.app</a> if you cannot reach the in-app deletion control or have questions about a pending request.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
